          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On January 3, 2009, at 20:10, a motorist and his passenger observed the rapid descent of a very bright yellow light point with no trailing behind the phenomenon. It quickly disappeared behind a hill. No particular noise was heard. A possible hypothesis is the observation of an atmospheric reentry, but in the absence of more precise information (in particular, no request for a PV), this observation lacks information to allow an investigation. The case is classified as \"C\".",
